# title: European put
# category: Vanillas and digitals
# underlyings: 1
# source: Black & Scholes, The Pricing of Options and Corporate Liabilities, Journal of Political Economy, 1973
# source: Hull, Options, Futures, and Other Derivatives, 11th ed., Pearson, ch. 15 (the Black-Scholes-Merton model)
# summary: The right to sell the stock at its strike level one year later: pays the fall of the stock below the strike, nothing if it ends above.
# param: strike = 1.0 | percent | Strike, % of the initial level
#
# Paid in the stock's currency, per share.

2027-01-04
    strike = 1.0
    s0 = spot()

2028-01-04
    pays max(strike * s0 - spot(), 0)
